(module easyeda2kicad:SOIC-8_L5.0-W4.0-P1.27-LS6.0-BL-EP2.0 (layer F.Cu) (tedit 5DC5F6A4)
	(attr smd)
	(descr "LM5017 SO PowerPAD-8 (TI DDA0008B), land pattern TI MRA08B Rev B, datasheet p.29. NAME IS STALE: the exposed pad is now 3.10 x 2.41mm (TI's recommended land, read off the RECOMMENDED LAND PATTERN drawing: (.122)[3.1] along the 1.27mm pitch axis, (.095)[2.41] along the 5.56mm row-span axis), NOT the 2.0 x 2.0mm the filename and the easyeda2kicad pull claim - the pulled EP was 46% undersized in area. 8 leads left as pulled (1.27mm pitch, 5.54mm row span, verified against TI's 1.27 / 5.56). 4 thermal vias 0.30mm drill / 0.61mm pad (0.155mm annulus, above the 0.15mm JLC floor) respread to +/-0.85, +/-0.65 under the enlarged EP; their *.Paste and *.Mask layers were REMOVED so they are tented on both faces - mandatory on this board because the bottom copper is a flat heatsink mounting face and a mask-opened via there would take solder and break flatness; tenting is also the standard anti-wicking mitigation for via-in-pad. EP paste aperture reduced 0.20mm per side (2.70 x 2.01 = 73% of the EP) against float/voiding. Courtyard corrected - the pull shipped one that cut through the lead pads.")
	(fp_text reference REF** (at 0 -4.614) (layer F.SilkS)
		(effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
	)
